SwiftPutty local patch 0018
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; should be (a damaged session aborts)

Settings: the two hand-loaded enum settings load an unknown saved value
as their default.

  - BugHMAC2 was loaded as 2 minus the saved number, unchecked: a saved
    value outside 0..2 gave a Conf value that save_open_settings could
    not map back, and saving failed the "unmapped integer value"
    assertion. Now mapped through conf_enum_auto_off_on, Auto if
    unknown.
  - ProxyMethod falls back to the old ProxyType; if neither held a known
    value, confval was used uninitialised (undefined behaviour, then the
    same assertion when saving). Now no proxy.

Applies after patch 0016. Found by fuzzing
(Core/tests/fuzz/fuzz_parsers.c).

--- a/settings.c
+++ b/settings.c
@@ -861,7 +861,9 @@
     /* proxy settings */
     {
         int storageval = gppi_raw(sesskey, "ProxyMethod", -1);
-        int confval;
+        /* No proxy if neither the current nor the old keyword holds a
+         * value we know (confval was left uninitialised then). */
+        int confval = PROXY_NONE;
         if (!conf_enum_map_from_storage(&conf_enum_proxy_type,
                                         storageval, &confval)) {
             /*
@@ -1046,9 +1048,15 @@
 
     gppmap(sesskey, "PortForwardings", conf, CONF_portfwd);
     {
-        int i;
-        i = gppi_raw(sesskey, "BugHMAC2", 0); conf_set_int(conf, CONF_sshbug_hmac2, 2-i);
-        if (2-i == AUTO) {
+        int i, confval;
+        /* Through the storage enum, so that a value out of range loads
+         * as the default rather than as a Conf value that
+         * save_open_settings cannot map back (an assertion failure). */
+        i = gppi_raw(sesskey, "BugHMAC2", 0);
+        if (!conf_enum_map_from_storage(&conf_enum_auto_off_on, i, &confval))
+            confval = AUTO;
+        conf_set_int(conf, CONF_sshbug_hmac2, confval);
+        if (confval == AUTO) {
             i = gppi_raw(sesskey, "BuggyMAC", 0);
             if (i == 1)
                 conf_set_int(conf, CONF_sshbug_hmac2, FORCE_ON);
